1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:06,500
Last year, Delta got $8.2 billion from
a company that doesn't fly a single

2
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:07,140
plane.

3
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:12,260
American Express. Every time someone
swipes a Delta credit card, Amex buys

4
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:14,981
miles from Delta. With real cash.

5
00:00:15,001 --> 00:00:18,501
That's more than Delta's
entire profit for the year.

6
00:00:18,521 --> 00:00:22,151
$6.2 billion, before taxes.

7
00:00:22,171 --> 00:00:27,471
And it's not just Delta. In 2020, United
borrowed against its miles program.

8
00:00:27,491 --> 00:00:30,533
It was valued at $22 billion.

9
00:00:30,553 --> 00:00:34,992
The whole airline, planes and
all, was worth about half that.

10
00:00:35,012 --> 00:00:37,072
Airlines don't just sell seats.

11
00:00:37,092 --> 00:00:41,001
They sell miles, to banks, by the billion.

12
00:00:41,021 --> 00:00:43,561
So every time you swipe for miles…

13
00:00:43,581 --> 00:00:45,391
the airline gets paid.
